From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:19:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] hexagonfs: refuse ".." above an assigned search
 directory

The parents of a search directory opened from the root are owned by that
directory's descriptor. A ".." that climbed out of it handed one of them
out under a new file number or freed it on an error path, leaving the
search directory pointing at freed memory. Such a ".." now fails with
EACCES; ".." from the root and from directories walked in the same path
works as before.

Create, unlink and rename refuse "." and ".." as the final component
with EISDIR.

Signed-off-by: seilent <github@seilent.net>
---
 hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs.c | 15 +++++++++------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs.c b/hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs.c
index 603a40a..f745aa9 100644
--- a/hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs.c
+++ b/hexagonrpcd/hexagonfs.c
@@ -167,7 +167,10 @@ int hexagonfs_openat(struct hexagonfs_fd **fds, int rootfd, int dirfd, const cha
 		if (!strcmp(segment, ".")) {
 			goto next;
 		} else if (!strcmp(segment, "..")) {
-			fd = pop_dir(fd, fds[rootfd]);
+			if (fd->is_assigned && fd != fds[rootfd])
+				ret = -EACCES;
+			else
+				fd = pop_dir(fd, fds[rootfd]);
 		} else {
 			ret = fd->ops->openat(fd, segment, expect_dir, &fd);
 		}
@@ -300,13 +303,13 @@ static int resolve_parent(struct hexagonfs_fd **fds, int rootfd, int dirfd,
 	int fileno;
 
 	*owned = false;
+	*base = slash == NULL ? name : slash + 1;
 
-	if (slash == NULL) {
-		*base = name;
-		return dirfd;
-	}
+	if (!strcmp(*base, ".") || !strcmp(*base, ".."))
+		return -EISDIR;
 
-	*base = slash + 1;
+	if (slash == NULL)
+		return dirfd;
 
 	if (slash == name)
 		return rootfd;
